WEBVTT

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:03.340
<i>...Airport saw a rush of...</i>

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.100
<b>A Rush of Travelers Returning Home After the Long Holiday</b>

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:04.650
<i>...by the minute...</i>

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:04.350
<b>New Year's Documentary 
2-hour Special</b>

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:04.350
<b>Sun Flares and Auroras Seen from the South Pole</b>

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:05.350
<b>Kamakura 
Strolling Without a Plan</b>

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:05.350
<b>In search of the famous Komachi Street 
shop with the legendary rice balls</b>

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:05.360
<i>The most popular...</i>

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.920
<i>...is our first guest of the new year!</i>

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.800
<i>Happy New Year!</i>

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.590
Hasn't the broadcast started yet?

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.970
<i>Thanks for having us! We're—</i>

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:18.070
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:19.900
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:27.020
Verse 18

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:27.020
The storm
 will soon
 carry me

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:27.550
<i>Both players continue to take cards 
with agility in the second match.</i>

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:31.860
<i>Our commentator is the head of
the Kyoto Myojo Society, Coach Ise.</i>

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:31.860
Classy     Like Ise lobster? 
Is he good at karuta? 
Crap, he's kind of my type 
But Watarai-san was so funny

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:35.440
<b>I feel at ease
 with him</b>

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:35.460
So the Queen reached Class A
when she was in the Myojo Society?

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:40.300
Yes, City Councilwoman Wakamiya
brought her to us,

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.820
and she was always a bit special.

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:43.200
She's good!

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.280
A ten-year-old kid won in Class B?!

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:47.410
She's the youngest Class A player in history!

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:51.940
Coach Ise told me that you reached Class A?

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:56.130
It's true! That's an incredible 
achievement in the world of karuta!

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:59.440
It seems you had a knack for it. Good for you.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:04.510
<i>There's never been any warmth 
in anything my grandma said.</i>

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:06.740
You're an attractive advertisement.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:08.560
<i>I'm not even disappointed.</i>

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:10.800
<i>My class trip...</i>

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:14.550
<i>Nothing... I feel nothing.</i>

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:19.570
Inokuma has 10, and the Queen has 15.

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:22.380
Isn't a five-card differential 
unusual for the Queen?

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:26.610
It could be that more of 
Inokuma-san's cards have been read,

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:28.490
but the momentum does seem to favor her.

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:32.920
<i>One card at a time...</i>

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:36.290
<i>Wakamiya-san doesn't use cross strokes.</i>

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:40.180
<i>"May I see" and "May I live,"
with Reader Hirota reading them...</i>

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:42.580
<i>May I see you...</i>

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:42.580
<i>I can take them on "I."</i>

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:45.850
She's widening her lead! 
Her speed is incredible!

00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:44.610
<i>Shinobu-chan...</i>

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:50.190
Because this will probably be 
my last Queen match.

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:54.010
I wish I could say I've yet to reach my peak,

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:57.980
but right now...
I think "right now" might be all I have.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:01.600
So right now, I'm going to give my all.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:04.610
This will sound cocky,

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:07.600
but I want to make a miracle happen.

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:11.910
For the girls who want to love 
karuta all their lives...

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:18.540
I want them to know that even if they 
have three kids, they can be Queen.

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:23.520
Let's play karuta again!

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:25.260
The Queen match!

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.270
<i>A class trip?</i>

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:32.270
<i>Shinobu-chan...</i>

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:34.820
<i>I...</i>

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:40.710
<i>I broke my promise.</i>

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:43.190
That was close!

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:48.040
She just can't seem to turn things around.

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:48.040
<i>Something's wrong. Something's wrong.</i>

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.610
This is a tough turn of events
for Queen Wakamiya.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.110
<i>Coach Ise...</i>

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:58.120
The more isolated she is,
the stronger she will become.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:01.380
<i>Coach Ise, you're such a liar.</i>

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:07.310
Could it be... Is the Queen really going to...

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:08.640
<i>I do not know where this love will take me</i>

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:13.660
<i>If I'm stronger the more isolated I am,</i>

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:19.780
<i>then shouldn't I be at 
my strongest right now?</i>

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:24.340
For the first time ever, Wakamiya Shinobu
has dropped a round in the Queen match.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:26.670
Her long winning streak is over.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:29.200
<i>What happened, Shinobu-chan?</i>

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:34.210
After the match, each player counts 
their cards to make sure there are 50

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:45.480
<i>The cards...</i>

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:48.530
<i>I have to...</i>

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:00.640
<i>Wait...</i>

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:02.510
<i>Wait.</i>

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:07.130
<i>Which cards did I have left at the end?</i>

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:10.020
<i>Which card did she take that made me lose?</i>

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.180
<i>Wait...</i>

00:05:11.790 --> 00:05:13.620
Taking all the cards
and turning them in...

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:13.630
Wait.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.120
is the winner's job

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:16.130
<i>Everyone...</i>

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:18.180
<i>Don't leave.</i>

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:28.500
<i>Inokuma won, huh? Drama, indeed...</i>

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:34.380
<i>In the sleepy...</i>

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:36.340
<i>The Master match is still continuing.</i>

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:38.420
Harada, grade 6, is leading.

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:38.610
<i>Now, hang on...</i>

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:40.120
<i>Is the Master in his right mind?</i>

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:43.340
<i>Said night was young...</i>

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:45.160
A-And here, too...

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:47.720
In the Master match, unbelievably,

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:49.470
the challenger wins!

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:52.000
Both Master and Queen will lose
their titles with one more loss.

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:54.240
They're both in check!

00:05:55.070 --> 00:05:56.120
Chihaya!

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:58.080
<i>Shinobu-chan!</i>

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:00.050
<i>Shinobu-chan!</i>

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:01.620
<i>Shinobu-chan!</i>

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:03.710
Kana-chan, help me!

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:06.540
What's going on, Chihaya-chan? 
You're in your socks—

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:08.580
Kana-chan, you have to help me
with Shinobu-chan!

00:06:10.630 --> 00:06:12.030
Who do you think will win?

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:13.440
I don't know anymore.

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:15.700
They weren't very focused toward the end.

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:16.390
Intriguing...

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:17.030
Who's your money on?

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:18.690
It'll be incredible if Inokuma-san wins.

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:20.180
I want to see the strong Wakamiya.

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:20.740
<i>It's too much noise.</i>

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:21.820
She has the momentum, too.

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:24.930
<i>The support, the expectations... all of it.</i>

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:28.190
Shinobu, open the door! Shinobu!

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:42.100
I'm fine. I just need to lie down.

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:44.030
Mommy's awesome! Mommy's awesome!

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:45.470
Want to eat something? You missed lunch.

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:45.020
Aki!

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:47.000
Hey, Mommy won! Were you watching?

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:49.710
No... I'll feel sick whether I eat or not.

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:49.710
Come outside!

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:52.130
No! I'm staying with Mommy!

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:52.720
But...

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:55.730
No! I wanna stay with Mommy!

00:06:53.170 --> 00:06:56.000
During the match, I felt so light,
it didn't seem real.

00:06:56.830 --> 00:06:58.490
Thank you.

00:06:57.420 --> 00:07:00.490
Mommy! I'm staying with Mommy!

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:01.570
Can I keep trying a little longer?

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:03.560
No! I wanna stay here!

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:05.070
Just one more...

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:06.800
Mommy!

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:08.490
<b>No! I'm staying here! Mommy!</b>

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:08.490
<b>Mommy needs to rest!</b>

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:08.100
This is good.

00:07:08.480 --> 00:07:11.160
When the first two rounds
 in a Queen match are split,

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:13.620
it goes on break while
the Master match has its third round.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:15.830
You have almost two hours to rest.

00:07:16.240 --> 00:07:18.910
Is Haruka-san all right?

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:21.130
I think she's fine.

00:07:21.130 --> 00:07:24.770
I didn't have this much morning 
sickness with Aki or Jin...

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:27.300
<b>Wobble</b>

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:27.520
I bet that means this is
the girl I've been hoping for!

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:29.210
That's what she said earlier.

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:29.720
Huh?!

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:31.870
It'll be fine.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:37.220
Of all the people I've played against,
she's the strongest.

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:40.580
That goes for her mind, her body,

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:42.900
and her feelings toward this.

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:51.810
So you're able to watch it now?

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:54.490
You're drinking, Tadashi-niichan?

00:07:56.790 --> 00:07:58.240
Wh-What about Yukiko-chan?

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:02.590
<i>She's at home, just watching TV.</i>

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:04.130
<i>We bought a 60-inch, y'know!</i>

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:04.880
Whatever.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:09.460
<i>We bought a 60-inch, but it's only about
the 30 square centimeters in the middle</i>

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:11.240
<i>that Yukiko-chan can see.</i>

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:16.300
For the third match,

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:19.980
our commentator is All Japan Karuta 
Association Chairman Mashita, grade 10.

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:19.970
<b>The chairman... What a relief...</b>

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:22.970
Since the Queen match is on break at this time,

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:22.980
<b>Couldn't get floor seats,
 stuck watching on the first floor</b>

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:25.370
our focus will be on the Master match.

00:08:25.820 --> 00:08:28.480
The challenger, Harada, grade 6, has two wins.

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:31.490
<b>So dull-looking lolol     Soooo dull... 
All old dudes     I like that, though 
Not much to look at 
Too dull lololol</b>

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:31.480
<i>One more win will make him the Master.</i>

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:33.940
It all comes down to this third match.

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:36.370
What sort of karuta will 
the two of them play?

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:36.370
Third Match Reader 
Certified Reader Igarashi

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:42.210
<i>The hazed early dawn mist 
over the Kawagiri River</i>

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:41.180
Wh-What?!

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:41.680
Harada, grade 6, protected the first card!

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:42.210
Huh?

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:44.520
I've never seen that before...

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:48.440
I've never seen the Master 
try to cover a card before.

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:49.610
That was a first?

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:51.220
He's awful at it!

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:52.720
<i>What was that?</i>

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:53.770
<i>What was that?</i>

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:54.930
<i>What was that?</i>

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:57.140
<i>Feel love deepen...</i>

00:08:56.450 --> 00:08:57.290
So fast!

00:08:57.290 --> 00:09:04.300
<i>When the misty bridge of magpie 
feathers comes into sight,</i>

00:08:57.940 --> 00:08:59.800
<i>Unlike in the first two matches,</i>

00:08:59.800 --> 00:09:01.710
<i>the Master is playing very aggressively!</i>

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:03.810
<i>He was playing rather lazily,</i>

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:06.670
<i>but perhaps because the cameras 
are on the Master match now,</i>

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:09.530
<i>he's turned on the turbo that 
he normally doesn't use.</i>

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:12.560
Chairman Mashita's too frank...

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:14.710
<i>Dr. Harada...</i>

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:50.720
<i>I guess...</i>

00:09:51.410 --> 00:09:55.400
<i>I love my grandma a lot 
more than I realized.</i>

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:57.490
<i>But...</i>

00:09:58.380 --> 00:09:59.690
<i>But...</i>

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:30.560
You're not supposed to 
walk down the center!

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:33.400
The center of the path leading up to a shrine...

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:36.660
is exclusively for the gods to walk on.

00:10:55.440 --> 00:11:01.520
<i>May the time we spend apart 
from one another be</i>

00:10:57.030 --> 00:10:57.740
Oh!

00:10:57.740 --> 00:11:01.010
The Master managed to take 
that one by covering it.

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:04.590
The Master is even going for
the multi-syllable cards in this third match.

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:07.360
The gap has widened to 9 versus 20.

00:11:07.360 --> 00:11:10.980
Perhaps he's more determined now 
than in the first two matches?

00:11:11.570 --> 00:11:14.750
Shinobu! Where in the world were you?

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:17.040
Why aren't you wearing your kimono?

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:18.630
I'm putting it on now.

00:11:18.630 --> 00:11:21.700
I can do it myself, so don't come in.

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:24.030
Honestly, that girl!

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:25.120
Now, now.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:27.980
Nothing wrong with letting out
your inner child now and then.

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:30.940
<i>All alone...</i>

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:30.500
So fast!

00:11:30.970 --> 00:11:34.360
He's looking to finish it quickly this time.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:36.500
C-Can he even pace himself like that?

00:11:36.810 --> 00:11:39.500
Yes, as despicable as it is.

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:41.760
That's why he's the Master.

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:43.370
<i>Shinobu-chan...</i>

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:48.180
<i>Shinobu-chan, let's show them</i>

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:50.290
<i>our strength.</i>

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:54.100
<i>The ones being controlled...</i>

00:11:56.170 --> 00:11:57.960
<i>will not be us.</i>

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:00.390
A 17-card differential!

00:12:00.390 --> 00:12:03.290
The Master wins the third match
by a wide margin!

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:04.270
<i>17 cards...</i>

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:04.270
He's strong!

00:12:04.530 --> 00:12:07.460
The Master has awakened,
and he's after his fifth consecutive title!

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:06.910
<i>When he's not goofing around, 
he can do this anytime.</i>

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:11.220
<i>He got that far ahead of Dr. Harada?</i>

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:20.220
It's the Queen!

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:21.020
How does she look?

00:12:21.020 --> 00:12:22.420
Inokuma has the momentum, right?

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:23.620
How will the third match go?

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:25.110
If she plays naively, she'll lose!

00:12:25.110 --> 00:12:26.190
She doesn't look too great...

00:12:26.190 --> 00:12:27.070
What's gonna happen?

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:28.250
Shinobu-chan!

00:12:28.520 --> 00:12:29.600
I made tasuki!

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:30.160
Huh?

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:33.280
Can I put them on you? They work 
the same on long sleeves!

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:33.560
There's no difference

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:40.900
<b>Sh-Shinobu's letting her do
 whatever she wants...</b>

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:44.280
Chihaya...

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:47.700
What were you praying for at the shrine?

00:12:48.710 --> 00:12:51.400
I prayed that Dr. Harada would be 
able to play at his full strength.

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:53.240
That's who you're rooting for?!

00:12:58.580 --> 00:13:01.260
<i>Well... As for me...</i>

00:13:04.920 --> 00:13:08.810
<i>I said I'd be coming to bring you all home.</i>

00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:15.620
Competitors, please enter the hall.

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:21.760
Hey, could you get me that?

00:13:20.520 --> 00:13:22.480
<b>Wife</b>

00:13:21.760 --> 00:13:23.100
You're going to use it?

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:24.650
<b>Poof</b>

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:32.100
All right, everyone... let's go!

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:34.580
Master Match
Fourth Round

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:34.580
Queen Match
Third Round

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:34.190
One match to go!

00:13:34.590 --> 00:13:37.960
You should be sleeping. Don't you 
have your tournament tomorrow?

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:41.390
<i>Dr. Harada...</i>

00:13:41.390 --> 00:13:43.720
<i>He really did throw the third match.</i>

00:13:44.270 --> 00:13:47.330
<i>The damn bear's actually using his head.</i>

00:13:47.330 --> 00:13:49.080
<i>Considering his stamina...</i>

00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:52.220
<i>The fourth match is the time to make it count.</i>

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:52.220
Wife: 
Doesn't understand the game well

00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:54.370
<i>Why?</i>

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:58.700
Our commentator is a former Queen 
and current certified reader,

00:13:58.700 --> 00:14:00.140
Yamashiro Kyoko-san.

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:01.820
She's beautiful♥

00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:01.870
Thank you for having me.

